00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.460
Now, here's something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.180
Want to know a secret about cosmos?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.920
Did you know that the Russian word cosmos and the English word cosmos

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.480
are actually the same word?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.640
They both come from the ancient Greek cosmos,

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.060
which meant the entire ordered universe.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.280
This word started in ancient Greece,

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.660
travelled through Latin and other languages,

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.020
and arrived in Russian and English with almost no change.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.620
But be careful.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.700
The Russian word magazine sounds like magazine,

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.480
but actually means shop.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.580
Next time you see the English word cosmos,

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.560
remember it excels in with cosmos.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.860
They both come from the Greek idea of a beautiful ordered word.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:46.040
That connection is your secret short cut to remember it for a while.

